// ============================================================ ch 1
= Chapter 1: Introduction

Chapter 1 states the purpose of this assessment, how it should be read, what it
covers, and the limits within which its findings hold. It closes with the data
sources on which every figure in the assessment rests.

== Purpose

This assessment identifies where #str(scope.budget) additional
#scope.unit#if scope.budget > 1 [s] should be placed in #scope.adm2 District so
as to bring the largest number of people currently without service inside a
#scope.unit service radius, and states what each of those placements would
achieve.

== How to Read this Assessment

Chapter 2 describes the current state of service in the district. Chapter 3
states how the assessment was carried out, including every retrieval made and
every cleaning rule applied. Chapter 4 gives the recommendation. Chapter 5
records the review, including each point at which a reviewing officer overruled
the analysis and what that decision cost. Chapter 6 tests how far the
recommendation depends on assumptions that can reasonably be changed.

Appendix A records properties of the source data that would have changed a
figure had they been read differently. Appendix B is the retrieval record.
Appendix C is the reproduction record.

== Scope and Applicability

This assessment covers #scope.adm2 District only. Coverage is computed against
#scope.unit records held in the source register; infrastructure that is not
recorded appears here as absence of service. The method is not specific to this
district or this domain, and the same procedure applies without modification to
health facility access, disease control and environmental monitoring.

== Limitations

+ *The register is not a census.* Coverage is computed against recorded
  #scope.unit#if scope.budget > 1 [s] only. Unmapped infrastructure appears as
  absence of service.
+ *Records age.* The median record for this district is
  #str(scope.median_record_age_years) years old. Findings describe the surveyed
  state of the network, not necessarily its state today.
+ *Distance is straight-line.* Terrain, watercourses and footpath networks are
  not modelled, so real walking distances exceed the radius used here.
+ *Costs are not modelled.* Rehabilitating an existing point and constructing a
  new one draw equally on the budget. Chapter 6 reports what changes when only
  rehabilitation is permitted.
+ *No field verification was performed.* No site in Chapter 4 has been visited.

== Decisions This Assessment Rests On

