= Chapter 6: Sensitivity

Chapter 6 tests how far the recommendation at Chapter 4 depends on assumptions
that a reviewing officer may reasonably wish to change. Each scenario re-solves
from the same retrieved data with a single assumption altered.

#if d.sensitivity.len() > 0 [
  #figure(
    gov-tbl(
      columns: (1fr, auto, auto, auto),
      align: (left, right, right, right),
      header: ([Scenario], [Covered], [Share], [Against base case]),
      rows: d.sensitivity.map(s => (
        s.label, thousands(s.covered), pct(s.share),
        (if s.delta > 0 { "+" } else { "" }) + thousands(s.delta) + " people"))),
    caption: [Sensitivity of the Recommendation],
  )

  #callout("Rehabilitation Against New Construction")[
    The base case does not select rehabilitation of existing
    #scope.unit#if scope.budget > 1 [s], because a location recorded as not
    serving generally stands beside one that is serving and therefore adds little
    new coverage. Rehabilitation is nonetheless materially cheaper per unit than
    new construction, and cost is not modelled in this assessment. Table 8 states
    what a rehabilitation-only programme of the same size would achieve, so the
    two can be weighed against costs held by the district.
  ]
] else [
  No sensitivity scenarios were run for this assessment.
]

